{
 "asset": "Node_el_camera_node_common",
 "about": "Camera nodes (tools/content/build_camera_sets.py, docs/research/31-battle-camera.md): the shots of the original battle footage, framed on the acting unit's bones (CharacterBoneList.Bone WAIST 1, SPINE2 4, NECK 5, HEAD 6), measured on every tactical action of the original footage: glides for normal attacks, cuts for skills and SPs (jdr_<shot>_0 is a pose, jdr_<shot>_<k> the delta to its next step: the client adds every later step's node to the first); the win, boss-intro and finish shots; ski_cam_00 (the client's test node) and jdr_side (the old world-fixed side view). Values are ours.",
